    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d372">

                <pb facs="0492" n="412" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg412"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The French minister for foreign affairs to Mr.
                        Cambon.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram presented by the French ambassador to the
                        President, May 12, 1902.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-05-11"><hi rendition="#italic">May 11,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Thank the Government of the United States for the sympathy evidenced by the
                    American people. It will never be forgotten in France.</p>
                <p>The whole of the island of Martinique and Fort de France are threatened. In order
                    to enable us to save the population you will please ask, as a national service,
                    of the American Government that it may see fit to send means of transportation
                    to Martinique (Fort de France) as soon as possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Delcassé.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
